# Opus Quad fixture: rekordbox-keep-alive
# Quoted bytes, not a capture: the keep-alive rekordbox sends in lighting
# mode, as published by two independent implementations that use it to
# make an Opus Quad talk to them:
#   https://github.com/Deep-Symmetry/beat-link/blob/main/src/main/java/org/deepsymmetry/beatlink/VirtualRekordbox.java
#     (array `rekordboxKeepAliveBytes`, the template before the MAC and IP are patched in)
#   https://github.com/kyleawayan/opus-quad-pro-dj-link-analysis/blob/main/pro-dj-link.js
#     (`sendKeepAlive()`, which yields the same bytes for this MAC and IP)
# Documented in: docs/protocols/opus-quad.md#joining-as-rekordbox-lighting
# Broadcast to port 50000: name "rekordbox", device 0x17, MAC 18:3e:ef:da:5b:ca,
# IP 192.168.2.11 (the values in the beat-link template).
# Bytes: UDP payload, hex, 16 per line.
51 73 70 74 31 57 6d 4a 4f 4c 06 00 72 65 6b 6f
72 64 62 6f 78 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
01 03 00 36 17 01 18 3e ef da 5b ca c0 a8 02 0b
04 01 00 00 04 08
